{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the earth brought forth grass, etc., after its kind.</b> In tractate חולין (דף ס' ע\"א) it expounds that the grasses grew a hundredfold on their own, etc.; the Sar Ha'Olam opened and said: ״יהי כבוד ה' לעולם״. And this is difficult for the one who says: Enoch — that is Metatron, and Metatron — that is the Sar Ha'Olam, for at that time Enoch had not yet been created. And some explain that there are two [entities called] Sar Ha'Olam. And further one may say: that [teaching] is not according to the one who says Enoch — that is Metatron; yet even according to him one may say: although he himself was not created, his soul or his mazal was nevertheless created, for that verse was said — as we find with the Book of the Generations of Adam, where we expound: this teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, showed [Adam] each generation and its sages; even though those generations had not yet been created, none the less their souls and their mazal He showed him."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:15:40.383144730Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}